{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"fearful-kindly-lynx","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe proposed deterministic clarity criteria need adversarial validation against this project ticket history. A rule that rejects a valid historical ticket is either unsound or requires a narrower applicability gate.\n\n## Approach\nSearch completed and accepted tickets for the strongest counterexample to each proposed rule, then inspect the full ticket and relevant review/completion evidence. Historical accepted tickets are the right corpus because they expose legitimate plan shapes that synthetic examples can miss.\n\n## Scope\nRead-only analysis of the rebar ticket store; no repository files will be modified.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each proposed deterministic criterion has a cited historical counterexample or an explicit statement that no counterexample was found; verified by ticket ids and quoted plan excerpts recorded in a ticket comment.\n- [ ] Each counterexample explains why the ticket remained valid and what false-positive mechanism the rule would trigger; verified by the recorded status, review evidence, or delivered outcome.\n- [ ] Each criterion is classified as retain, narrow, advisory-only, or reject based on the evidence; verified by a structured recommendation table in the recorded findings.\n- [ ] Findings are recorded on this ticket; verified by the presence of the final analysis comment.","id":"3575-c189-22ce-4166","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["analysis","clarity","plan-review"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Find historical false positives for proposed clarity criteria"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785189815058926001,"uuid":"6ae5c723-97bc-44e0-b6ae-cf7113098b65"}